      "text": [
        " سُئِلَ أَبُو عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) عَنْ قَاضٍ بَيْنَ قَرْيَتَيْنِ يَأْخُذُ مِنَ السُّلْطَانِ عَلَى الْقَضَاءِ الرِّزْقَ فَقَالَ ذَلِكَ السُّحْتُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Mahboub, from Abdullah Bin Sinan who said, ",
          "‘Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> was asked about a judge between two towns taking the livelihood from the ruling authorities upon the judgements. So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘That is the ill-gotten (forbidden)’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "1. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn Mahbub from ‘ Abd Allah ibn Sinan who has narrated the following: “Once abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, was asked about a judge between two towns who receives his wages from al-Sultan. He (the Imam) said, ‘It is a sinful earning.”’ "
        ]
      }
    },
